course: dictionary
lesson: 15240
title: Shears: a tool and a action word
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one job. «Shears» can name a tool, or it can tell you what someone does. Look at the words around it to see which job it has. Ask: is it a thing, or is somebody doing something?
explain: «Dad used garden shears to trim the hedge.» Here shears is a thing. The words «garden» and «trim the hedge» tell you it is a tool, like big, strong scissors for cutting.
explain: «The farmer shears the sheep every spring.» Here shears is an action. The farmer is doing something to the sheep, and the word «sheep» tells you what he cuts: their wool.
fact: Shears is a tool like big, strong scissors. You use it for cutting hedges, grass, metal or sheep's wool.
fact: «A pair of shears» is the usual way to name the tool, because shears has two blades.
fact: «Shears» can also be a verb, so «the farmer shears the sheep» means he cuts off their wool.
fact: The past form of the verb is «sheared», as in «the farmer sheared the sheep last week».
fact: Shears are very sharp, so they are for adults to use. Keep them away from little children.
exercise: «Dad used garden shears to trim the hedge.» What are shears in this sentence? | A kind of garden seat | A bird that sings | A cooking pot | *A large cutting tool like big, strong scissors
exercise: «The farmer shears the sheep every spring.» What does shears mean here? | Paints them | Waters them | Feeds them hay | *Cuts off their wool
exercise: In «She bought a pair of shears», what kind of word is shears? | An adjective | *A noun | A question word | A verb
test: Which phrase names a tool for cutting a hedge? | *hedge shears | hedge sleeping | hedge painting | hedge singing
test: Yesterday the farmer ___ the sheep. Pick the right verb form. | *sheared | shear | shears | shearing
exam: Which sentence uses shears as a verb? | Put the shears on the shelf. | *The farmer shears the sheep. | The shears were in the box. | The shears are sharp.
